  <section>
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">The RocketBooster family</p>
    <h1 class="page-title mt-3">Tools for Rocket.rs, the Rust web framework</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-text">Latest Release: 🎉 Propel v0.2.0 (Nov 9, 2026) · Ignite v0.3.0 (Nov 14, 2026) · Orbit v0.1.0 (Nov 11, 2026)</p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg">The RocketBooster family has three projects. Propel is the templating engine that renders the views. Ignite is an admin panel for Rocket, and it is built on Propel templates. Orbit is the database layer.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="panel">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-heading">Propel</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">The templating engine. Propel is a Blade-inspired templating system for Rocket.rs. Templates compile to typed Rust views, so a view's structure is checked when the app is built.</p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        <a target="_new" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/lajennylove/Propel" class="text-link">Propel on GitHub</a> · <a href="https://propel.rocketboost.rs" class="text-link">Propel docs</a> · <a target="_new" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/lajennylove/RocketPropel" class="text-link">Propel example</a>
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-heading">Ignite</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">The admin panel. Ignite builds a back office for a MariaDB or MySQL table: a sign-in page, a dashboard, and screens to list, search, sort, create, edit and delete its rows.</p>
      <p class="mt-3">Ignite is in development. Its docs say which parts are built and which are not yet.</p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        <a target="_new" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/lajennylove/Ignite" class="text-link">Ignite on GitHub</a> · <a href="https://ignite.rocketboost.rs" class="text-link">Ignite docs</a> · <a target="_new" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/lajennylove/RocketIgniteExample" class="text-link">Ignite example</a>
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-heading">Orbit</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">The database layer. Orbit is an ORM for Rocket.rs apps, starting with MySQL and MariaDB. It maps tables to Rust types, with a query builder, transactions and migrations.</p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        <a target="_new" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/lajennylove/Orbit" class="text-link">Orbit on GitHub</a> · <a href="https://orbit.rocketboost.rs" class="text-link">Orbit docs</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

